1305	\begin{lemma}[Formalization support for the arguments of a supported CL function]\label{lem:cl-supported-restriction}
1306		\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.CondLinearTerm.eval_coordinateRestriction}
1307		\leanok
1308		\uses{def:cl-func, def:register-subspace}
1309		This is not a named statement of the source article; it isolates a step used in the Lean proofs of Lemma~\ref{lem:cl-func-prod} and Lemma~\ref{lem:cl-dist-prod}. Let $S$ be a register subspace of $V$ and let $L$ be a CL function on $V$ all of whose factor spaces are contained in $S$. Then $L(x^S) = L(x)$ for every $x \in V$.
1310	\end{lemma}
1311	\begin{proof}
1312		\leanok
1313		\uses{def:cl-func}
1314		Induction on the level of $L$: the value of $L$ depends on $x$ only through the projections of $x$ onto the factor spaces of $L$, and $x^S$ and $x$ have the same projection onto every register subspace contained in $S$.
